<title>SWITZERLAND: UK bank says gold row won't stop German EMU entry.</title>
<headline>UK bank says gold row won't stop German EMU entry.</headline>
<dateline>FLIMS, Switzerland 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The row between the Bundesbank and the German government over the revaluation of gold and currency reserves will not affect Germany's commitment to the European single currency, said George Mathewson, chief executive of the Royal Bank of Scotland, on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;I think it only makes a difference in terms of it being a political issue. Technical issues are not going to stop them going in,&quot; he said in an interview with Reuters at a banking seminar organised by NCR Corp.</p>
<p>&quot;Whether they capitalise their gold or not, does it really make any difference to the issues?&quot; he added.</p>
<p>The Bundesbank and the German government entered open conflict on Wednesday as the central bank rejected Bonn's plans to revalue its assets, but the government said it would go ahead regardless.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
